# HYG drift report — plan_llvm_hyg.oot vs disk (2026-08-19)

File: openOODA/audit/hyg_drift_2026_08_19.oot

Logline: plan_llvm_hyg.oot is stale; llvm_emit_match_expr.oo grew +29 lines and llvm_emit_expr.oo grew +20 lines, and even the "fresh" plan_llvm_resi_hyg.oot is off by +11 on expr, so a HYG file is a snapshot not a live measure.

Setup: this report is part of the 2026-08-19 audit repair pass. Ground truth = on-disk .oo files under ooda/oodac/. Both HYG .oot files in audit/ are read-only inputs to this report. I do not edit them; this file only characterizes drift.

Beats:
  1. List every file mentioned in plan_llvm_hyg.oot and the count it claims.
  2. Cross-check against plan_llvm_resi_hyg.oot claims.
  3. Read the two .oo files in scope and report actual on-disk line counts.
  4. Name the HYG rot pattern and pick a fix.

